  "artifact": {
    "description": "Sole Menu",
    "text": "CLICK A ROW\n88\nWelcome to Solo\n+\nClick here first\n4 Dev server\n+ Auto-restart\n+ researcher\n+ writer\nrestwer\n+ Notifications\n+ Agents and terminals\norchestrator\nfetcher\nsummarizer\n+ claude-test-2-c\nDemo 1\n0:20\nCURVE SHARPNESS\nLoose\n(16)\nMedium\n(8)\nSharp (4)\nCorner\n(1)\nTransition zone\n8\nThe \"transition zone\" is how many pixels above and\nbelow the corner point the bezier control points are\nplaced. Smaller = sharper bend. At 1px the curve is\nessentially a rounded corner; at 16px it's the loose S-\ncurve from before.\nIn code: each curve C x1 y1, x2 y2, x y uses\ncontrol points where y1 = cornery - zone and y2 =\ncornery + zone , with both x's set to the entry/exit\ncolumns respectively.",
